bench/AOM_v0/rf_model_leaves/SPEC.md:14:`RFModelLeavesRegressor` proposes a complementary diagnostic: a Random Forest whose leaves contain *fast spectroscopic models* (PLS / Ridge / AOM-PLS-compact) instead of constant predictions. The tree learns a *routing* over samples on the basis of low-dimensional projections (PCA scores, AOM-PLS scores, or metadata); each leaf then fits a small expert on the full spectra of the samples it contains. At prediction time, a sample is routed through every tree to its leaves and the per-leaf expert predictions are bagged.
bench/AOM_v0/rf_model_leaves/SPEC.md:35:    leaf_model="pls",                # "pls" | "ridge" | "aom_pls_compact" | "fixed_mean"
bench/AOM_v0/rf_model_leaves/SPEC.md:54:1. **Routing-feature construction**. Build `X_route ∈ R^(n × d_route)` from `X` (and optional metadata). Default: `PCA(n_components=n_routing_components).fit_transform(StandardScaler(X))`. Alternatives: AOM-PLS scores from a pre-fitted ASLS-AOM-compact-cv5, or a user-supplied callable `routing_features(X) → R^(n × d_route)`.
bench/AOM_v0/rf_model_leaves/SPEC.md:61:   2. If `|I_{t,ℓ}| ≥ min_for(leaf_model)`, fit `leaf_model` on `(X[I_{t,ℓ}], y[I_{t,ℓ}])`. Hyperparameters come from `leaf_model_params`. AOM-PLS-compact runs its own internal CV on `I_{t,ℓ}` via `ASLS-AOM-compact-cv5-numpy`'s default config.
bench/AOM_v0/rf_model_leaves/SPEC.md:65:`min_for(leaf_model)` defaults: PLS=15 (need ≥3 components × ≥5 samples), Ridge=8, AOM-PLS-compact=30, fixed_mean=1.
bench/AOM_v0/rf_model_leaves/SPEC.md:91:- Per-leaf AOM-PLS-compact runs its own inner CV inside `I_{t,ℓ}`, which is strictly a subset of the outer training set; this preserves the nested boundary.
