+computed from benchmark result tables produced by the public repositories
+announced in the main manuscript.  The regression cohort contains 61 manifest
+rows; QUARTZ-style near-zero denominators are retained for absolute-error
+diagnostics but excluded from ratio tests.  The classification cohort contains
+17 manifest rows, with one row excluded from the AOM-PLS-DA paired analysis
+because the expected train/test file names differ from the benchmark runner
+convention.  Completed cartesian-HPO overlaps are 36 PLS datasets and 35
+Ridge datasets.
+
+Multi-seed evidence is aggregated at dataset level before paired tests.
+AOM-PLS, PLS-default, Ridge-default, PLS-HPO and Ridge-HPO use seeds
+0, 1 and 2 where the corresponding benchmark rows completed.  The AOM-Ridge
+headline selectors are reported on the deterministic headline run with
+random state 0, while the supplementary seed-stability table reports the
+available multi-seed AOM-PLS and AOM-Ridge diagnostics.  The main regression
+comparisons use paired dataset-level RMSEP ratios, Wilcoxon signed-rank tests
+where applicable and Holm correction within the reported comparison family.
+Classification comparisons use paired balanced-accuracy differences with the
+same family-wise correction.  The validation status of the software artifacts
+is summarized in Table~\ref{tab:sup_software}.
 
